WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.272
This browser example uses EXPLAIN to build the habit of inspecting a plan.

00:00:04.272 --> 00:00:10.032
Spark EXPLAIN output is different and usually more detailed, but the habit is the same.

00:00:10.032 --> 00:00:12.427
Do not guess what the engine is doing.

00:00:12.427 --> 00:00:19.337
Inspect the planned operators and look for scans, filters, joins, aggregates, sorts, and exchanges.

00:00:19.337 --> 00:00:26.257
Spark transformations are often lazy: they build a logical plan rather than immediately processing every row.

00:00:26.257 --> 00:00:32.247
An action triggers execution. That gives Spark an opportunity to optimize the plan.

00:00:32.247 --> 00:00:38.402
Develop the habit of reading EXPLAIN output and asking which operations cause scans, shuffles, sorts,

00:00:38.402 --> 00:00:39.920
or exchanges.
